The Unified Cyber Ontology
--------------------------

src/uco/schema/uco*.yaml, src/uco/datamodel/ and project/ render the
Unified Cyber Ontology (UCO) 1.5.0, which the UCO Community publishes at
https://github.com/ucoProject/UCO. They are this project's rendering,
written by scripts/uco_to_linkml.py from UCO's own files; they are not
the UCO Community's, and their use does not imply endorsement by it.
The description of each UCO class, property and vocabulary in them is
UCO's rdfs:comment text for that term, and each class, property and
vocabulary keeps its UCO IRI.

src/uco/schema/upstream/ holds a copy of UCO's ontology files, the
fifteen namespaces under ontology/uco/, the master ontology uco.ttl and
ontology/co/co.ttl, retrieved from
https://github.com/ucoProject/UCO/tree/7ebb3957e9e9a2e1bb9c66cd1ede8c912a726344
(the 1.5.0 release), beside the LICENSE from the root of the same commit.
Each file is identical to its counterpart there, and
scripts/check_upstream_release.py checks that they stay so. UCO is
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; its LICENSE holds the
licence text without a copyright line, and the repository carries no
NOTICE file of its own (both read on 2026-10-31). The tests also derive
example data from UCO's examples under tests/examples/ at that commit,
which are under the same licence. Nothing in this repository changes the
copied files.

lmodel/collections and the Collections Ontology
-----------------------------------------------

src/uco/schema/collections/collections.yaml is the schema module of the
Collections Ontology LinkML schema of lmodel/collections
(https://github.com/lmodel/collections) at release v0.1.0 (commit
a55334d11fdff610988c1c1776fcc3055295d74d), under the Apache License,
Version 2.0, copied unchanged. tests/test_collections_import.py pins its
git object hash. It renders the Collections Ontology (CO) 2.0 by Paolo
Ciccarese and Silvio Peroni, http://purl.org/co, which they describe in
"The Collections Ontology: creating and handling collections in OWL 2 DL
frameworks", Semantic Web 5(6), 2014, https://doi.org/10.3233/SW-130121.
The module keeps CO's names and IRIs. Its descriptions are
lmodel/collections' own words, and its use does not imply endorsement by
CO's authors.

lmodel/collections' NOTICE states the position on CO's licence. CO's
repository (https://github.com/collections-ontology/collections-ontology)
states no licence of its own. The Google Code archive's record of the
project, https://code.google.com/archive/p/collections-ontology, gives the
Apache License, Version 2.0, for its code, CO's OWL file among it, and
Creative Commons Attribution 3.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/) for its other content, such
as its wiki. The module cites one page of that wiki for a fact and copies
none of its text. This repository copies none of CO's own files: the
ontology/co/co.ttl named above is UCO's, which adds SHACL shapes to CO.

